A menu of actions opened from a button.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/dropdown-menu)

<%= embed UI::DropdownMenuPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
DropdownMenu do
  DropdownMenuTrigger { |trigger| Button(**trigger, variant: :outline) { "Open" } }
  DropdownMenuContent do
    DropdownMenuGroup do
      DropdownMenuGroupLabel { "My Account" }
      DropdownMenuItem { "Profile" }
      DropdownMenuItem { "Billing" }
    end
    DropdownMenuSeparator()
    DropdownMenuLinkItem(href: settings_path) { "Settings" }
  end
end
```

- `DropdownMenuTrigger` - toggles the menu; a block with an argument receives its attributes for your own Button.
- `DropdownMenuContent` - the popup, opened in the browser's top layer (so no `overflow` clips it) and placed by
  `side:` / `align:`, flipping at the viewport edge.
- `DropdownMenuItem` - an action; `DropdownMenuLinkItem` - a link.
- `DropdownMenuCheckboxItem`, `DropdownMenuRadioGroup` + `DropdownMenuRadioItem` - stateful options.
- `DropdownMenuGroup` / `DropdownMenuGroupLabel` / `DropdownMenuSeparator` - structure.
- `DropdownMenuSub` / `DropdownMenuSubTrigger` / `DropdownMenuSubContent` - nested submenus.

Tag a leading icon `data: { icon: "start" }`; push a trailing Kbd or Badge to the edge with `class: "ms-auto"`. Items
emit `ui--dropdown-menu:select`; wire an action with Stimulus, or use a link item or `button_to` inside the menu. To
pick a value use a [Select](<%= page_path(:select) %>); for right-click use a
[Context Menu](<%= page_path(:context_menu) %>); for an app command bar a [Menubar](<%= page_path(:menubar) %>).

